A||||15||Loki||LS1  or LT1?||||1||
Z||000000||Loki||06-12-2000||07:08 PM||||  Im considering doing a v8 in my 85 GT.. What is the difference between the above engines and which one would ork better in a Fiero?<P>Loki||||reg||1
Z||000001||DaRkLoRD||06-12-2000||07:54 PM||||Ork.. now there's a cool word.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||12
Z||000002||mrfixit58||06-12-2000||08:09 PM||||I may get this backwards but the LS1 is a conventional SBC with cast iron block, aluminum heads and reverse cooling (reverse from early SBC). The LT1 is a completely different motor design and will not share any parts with the early SBC and has a aluminum block and heads.<P>Roy||||reg||1
Z||000003||HYPTNOTiSE||06-12-2000||08:21 PM||||yes you have it backwards.  The LS-1 is a completely new engine. It's BAD ASS!!!  It uses all lightwieght stuff, no distributer, the camshaft is rifle bored to save weight, and is actually a composite type cam, it uses one shaft and you add lobes to the shaft.  If you want an LS-1 in you fiero, call archie, he's supposed to be the first person to do it, not sure if he's done yet or not, but i think this setup would cost well over $8K<P>Mike LeCompte||||reg||1
Z||000004||BN Boomer||06-12-2000||08:48 PM||||Aren't they <B>both</B> substantially different than the traditional SBC? Isn't the LT-1 that Chevrolet reincarnated an overhead cam motor? Do I know what I'm talking about?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Personally, if I were putting a V-8 into a Fiero, and it is one of my long term goals, I would go with the 355hp ZZ4 crate motor from GM Performance. They run around $3200 brand new.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Zman302||06-12-2000||11:11 PM||||The LT1 is pretty much the old small block.  It has the cast iron block and alum. heads.  The LS1 is a alum. block/heads.  It has all the goodies like the lightweight crank and pistons.  If i was going to go with one or the other i would most likely go with the LT1 for the fact that they are pretty common anymore and alot less complicated than the LS1.  Plus, even if you get one of the first couple yrs of the new LT1, you will get atleast 275 bhp which in a fiero would be plenty.  Either way you go, your gonna have a great time cruising that machine and seeing all those rice rockets in the rear view mirror.  ||||reg||1
Z||000006||olympic||06-12-2000||11:57 PM||||  LS1's were introduced in '97 so finding one may be difficult.  They were all aluminum and put out over 330 hp stock.  A real killer engine!!||||reg||1
Z||000007||2birds||06-13-2000||12:27 AM||||If you want a fuelie SBC in a Fiero, a TPI 305/350 (pre-93) will it easier than a LT1, due to the LT1 ignition wires coming out where the water pump normally is on a regular SBC.  Even with moving the transaxle to the left, it won't clear without notching the rear body rails.  With a normal SBC, you can use V8Archies pulley relocator version.<BR> <BR>I haven't done it myself, so I may be out of line here, but I saw the LT1 install attempt up close, and it wasn't real pretty.  <P>V8Archie has a pretty good site for info, and a decent rep from what I've seen here.  <P>Comments from the Batcave?||||reg||1
Z||000008||Dan86gt3.8||06-13-2000||03:30 AM||||yeah if you go ls1 it is going to cost you out the azz!  I think the price for a new crate ls1 is around 7k.  I have also emailed archie before about progress on the ls1 swap is going and he is slow to respond and when he does its vauge, which leads me to believe that things aren't going to well and theres lots of problems.  Also the ls1's heads are better and it has a 8 coil packs, one for each cylinder.  The lt1 has a different intake, the heads aren't as good and it still uses a distributor.  The ls1 also can be overhyped some, in the f-bod world the guys that are doing heads and cam lt1's are doing the same as the ls1 heads and cam cars but stock the ls1 is better and also lighter.  But there is more stuff for the lt1 and it would be alott esier to find cause look for f-dods 94-97 and whatever yhears they came in vettes.  Thats all I can think of for now.....||||reg||1
Z||000009||Monkeyman||06-13-2000||11:17 AM||||I wonder how much horsepower you could get out of 4,000 D cell batteries.||||reg||1
Z||000010||88GT3||06-13-2000||01:11 PM||||I think that would depend on how many stickers you had on the side ofyour car.  The more stickers the more horsepower. LOL||||reg||1
